  "credit": "© NASA / GSFC / SwRI / Lockheed Martin — public domain. First mission to the Jupiter Trojans — primordial asteroids co-orbiting Jupiter at the L4 and L5 Lagrange points, believed to preserve material from the outer protoplanetary disc. First asteroid flyby: Dinkinesh (2023-11-01), at which the contact-binary satellite Selam was discovered. Bonus main-belt asteroid Donaldjohanson flyby 2025-04. Eurybates encounter 2027-08; Patroclus-Menoetius binary 2033-03 closes the primary mission.",
